cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use quantum-cortex, its continuity benchmarks, or any derivative work, please cite it as below and retain the NOTICE file (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(d))."
title: "quantum-cortex: an open language model built to measure continuity"
abstract: "A 27 million parameter byte level language model with a memory outside its weights: a sealed journal of episodes that the model must cite or abstain from, built so that every claim about it has a row, a file and a test that can fail. The v1.1.0 edition carries the record up to row 54 (the organ's lifecycle on journals of eleven thousand and one hundred and ten thousand entries, the independent test on sealed families, the simple references and the cost) and the provenance benchmark module. Independent member of the Quantum Meridian ecosystem."
